Patch-Source: https://github.com/frenzymadness/pygame/commit/4113984c90f8fe2acf93924fd60147071cb5c444 (https://github.com/pygame/pygame/pull/4912)
From 4113984c90f8fe2acf93924fd60147071cb5c444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumir Balhar <lbalhar@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:06:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Cython 3.3 compatibility: remove illegal __dict__
 assignment in __cinit__

Cython 3.3.0 made accessing cdef __dict__ directly an error when the
attribute is declared in an extension type. The self.__dict__ = {}
initialization in Sprite.__cinit__ is now rejected. Removing it is safe
because Cython initializes the __dict__ slot automatically when
cdef dict __dict__ is declared.
---
 src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx b/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx
index 52d0c984..44cbbe89 100644
--- a/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx
+++ b/src_c/cython/pygame/_sprite.pyx
@@ -145,7 +145,6 @@ cdef class Sprite:
     cdef dict __dict__
 
     def __cinit__(self):
-        self.__dict__ = {}
         self.__g = set() # The groups the sprite is in
 
     def __init__(self, *groups):
-- 
2.56.0

